<title>UK: Booker sells forestry units for six mln stg.</title>
<headline>Booker sells forestry units for six mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Booker Plc said it had sold the forestry businesses and assets of Tilhill Economic Forestry Limited to UPM-Kymmene Corporation of Finland through its subsidiary Shotton Paper Company for six million stg.</p>
<p>It said the total paid was subject to completion adjustment and 5.5 million stg would be payable on completion, which is expected to be December 27.</p>
<p>Booker said in a statement that the sale completed its strategic withdrawal from land use management in Britain.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
